  "title": "mold 3.0 rewrote the high-speed linker in Rust",
  "narration": "mold 3.0 replaced its C++ codebase with Rust. This is the high-speed linker, not a developer fragrance. Maintainers say performance stays on par with mold 2.42.1. It keeps the same command-line options and target architectures. The rewrite focuses on safety and maintainability. Corrupted inputs now hit bounds checks instead of unsafe reads. The build system also moved from CMake to Cargo. Rust 1.95 or newer is required. The team tested every supported target and built all Gentoo packages. They reported no compatibility regressions. mold still wants to close more GNU ld compatibility gaps. Same speed, different language, fewer segmentation-fault-shaped surprises.",
